          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Notes for local identification: Colonies are encrusting to sub-massive. Polyps are mostly spaced on the colony surface. Tentacles are brownish-green and mostly extended during the day. Corallites are bigger than in L. pruinosa (some corallites with more than 5 mm width). Abundance: rare. Depth of occurrence: About 3 m.",
